{%- comment -%}
  Chemistrie Ritual Finder — implements the quiz logic documented in
  "Chemistrie Ritual Finder — Quiz logic & product mapping" (source: the
  GoHighLevel workflow "Chemistrie | Ritual Finder Processing", Sep 29 2026).

  Six questions plus a contact capture. Only two of them decide the outcome:
  Q1 sets the Ritual, Q4 sets the Tier, and Ritual x Tier resolves to a named
  set in MATRIX below. Q5 saves a secondary product without changing that set.
  Q2, Q3 and Q6 are collected for the profile only.

  This is deliberately separate from sections/ritual-finder-app.liquid, which
  is an older four-question quiz with different ritual names and still runs on
  the Ritual page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign velvet_prod = all_products['velvet']
  assign veil_prod = all_products['veil']
  assign cashmere_prod = all_products['cashmere']
  assign aura_prod = all_products['aura']
  assign silken_prod = all_products['silken']

  if velvet_prod == blank or veil_prod == blank or cashmere_prod == blank or aura_prod == blank or silken_prod == blank
    for col in collections
      for p in col.products
        assign ph = p.handle | downcase
        if velvet_prod == blank and ph contains 'velvet'
          assign velvet_prod = p
        elsif veil_prod == blank and ph contains 'veil'
          assign veil_prod = p
        elsif cashmere_prod == blank and ph contains 'cashmere'
          assign cashmere_prod = p
        elsif aura_prod == blank and ph contains 'aura'
          assign aura_prod = p
        elsif silken_prod == blank and ph contains 'silken'
          assign silken_prod = p
        endif
      endfor
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Images come from snippets/product-image-asset.liquid, the same approved
  theme assets the product page and collection grid use — the Shopify product
  images are not the approved shots, so featured_image renders placeholders.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture img_velvet -%}{%- render 'product-image-asset', product: velvet_prod -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture img_silken -%}{%- render 'product-image-asset', product: silken_prod -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture img_aura -%}{%- render 'product-image-asset', product: aura_prod -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture img_veil -%}{%- render 'product-image-asset', product: veil_prod -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture img_cashmere -%}{%- render 'product-image-asset', product: cashmere_prod -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img_velvet = img_velvet | strip | default: 'product-velvet.jpg'
  assign img_silken = img_silken | strip | default: 'product-silken.jpg'
  assign img_aura = img_aura | strip | default: 'product-aura.jpg'
  assign img_veil = img_veil | strip | default: 'product-veil.jpg'
  assign img_cashmere = img_cashmere | strip | default: 'product-cashmere.jpg'
-%}

<section class="gfinder" id="gift-ritual-finder" data-screen-label="Ritual Finder">
  <div class="gfinder__inner">
    <div class="gfinder__head">
      <span class="eyebrow">— {{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'Ritual Finder' }} —</span>
      <h2 class="display-h gfinder__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="gfinder__card" data-gfinder
      {%- if section.settings.webhook_url != blank %} data-endpoint="{{ section.settings.webhook_url }}"{% endif -%}
    >
      <div class="gfinder__progress" data-gf-progress>
        <span class="gfinder__progress-label">Question <b data-gf-current>1</b> of <span data-gf-total>6</span></span>
        <span class="gfinder__progress-track"><i data-gf-bar></i></span>
      </div>

      <div data-gf-steps>
        {%- comment -%} Q1 — sets the Ritual {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step is-active" data-gf-step data-gf-key="improve">
          <legend class="gfinder__q">What would you most like to improve about your skin?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Hydration">Hydration</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Texture">Texture</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Appearance of Fine Lines">Appearance of Fine Lines</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Uneven Tones">Uneven Tones</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Appearance of Scars">Appearance of Scars</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Overall Skin Maintenance">Overall Skin Maintenance</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Q2 — profile only {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step" data-gf-step data-gf-key="skin_type" hidden>
          <legend class="gfinder__q">How would you describe your skin?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Dry">Dry</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Normal">Normal</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Combination">Combination</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Oily">Oily</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Not Sure">Not Sure</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Q3 — profile only {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step" data-gf-step data-gf-key="sensitivity" hidden>
          <legend class="gfinder__q">How sensitive is your skin?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Rarely reacts">Rarely reacts</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Occasionally becomes irritated or sensitive">Occasionally becomes irritated or sensitive</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Frequently becomes irritated or sensitive">Frequently becomes irritated or sensitive</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="I'm not sure">I&rsquo;m not sure</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Q4 — sets the Tier {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step" data-gf-step data-gf-key="routine_fit" hidden>
          <legend class="gfinder__q">What kind of skincare routine fits your lifestyle?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Keep It Simple">Keep It Simple</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Balanced Routine">Balanced Routine</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Give Me The Full Ritual">Give Me The Full Ritual</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Q5 — saves a secondary product, does not change the set {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step" data-gf-step data-gf-key="secondary" hidden>
          <legend class="gfinder__q">What else would you like your skincare routine to focus on?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Hydration">Hydration</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Texture">Texture</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Appearance of fine lines">Appearance of fine lines</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Uneven tone">Uneven tone</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Appearance of scars">Appearance of scars</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Overall skin maintenance">Overall skin maintenance</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Nothing else, just my primary goal">Nothing else, just my primary goal</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Q6 — profile only {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="gfinder__step" data-gf-step data-gf-key="current_routine" hidden>
          <legend class="gfinder__q">What does your skincare routine look like today?</legend>
          <div class="gfinder__opts">
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Cleanser only or very minimal">Cleanser only or very minimal</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Cleanser + moisturizer">Cleanser + moisturizer</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="A few targeted products">A few targeted products</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="Full multi-step routine">Full multi-step routine</button>
            <button type="button" data-gf-opt="I don't currently have a consistent routine">I don&rsquo;t currently have a consistent routine</button>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%} Contact capture {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="gfinder__step gfinder__step--contact" data-gf-contact hidden>
          <p class="gfinder__q">Your Chemistrie ritual is ready.</p>
          <p class="gfinder__sub">Tell us where to send your personalized Chemistrie recommendation.</p>
          <div class="gfinder__fields">
            <label class="gfinder__field">
              <span>First Name</span>
              <input type="text" data-gf-name required autocomplete="given-name">
            </label>
            <label class="gfinder__field">
              <span>Email</span>
              <input type="email" data-gf-email required autocomplete="email">
            </label>
          </div>
          <p class="gfinder__error" data-gf-error hidden></p>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary gfinder__submit" data-gf-submit>Show my ritual</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gfinder__nav" data-gf-nav>
        <button type="button" class="gfinder__back" data-gf-back hidden>&larr; Back</button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Result {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="gfinder__result" data-gf-result hidden>
        {%- comment -%}
          Laid out to fit one desktop screen: title and the add-to-cart action
          share the top row; photo, ritual list and the "why we chose this"
          card share the middle row; the remaining cards sit in one row below.
          Stacks on narrower screens.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="gfinder__result-head">
          <div class="gfinder__result-heading">
            <span class="gfinder__result-eyebrow" data-gf-result-eyebrow>Your ritual</span>
            <h3 class="display-h gfinder__result-title" data-gf-result-title></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="gfinder__result-actions">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" data-gf-add>Add the ritual to cart</button>
            <a class="gfinder__restart" href="#" data-gf-restart>Start again</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gfinder__result-grid">
          <div class="gfinder__shot" data-gf-shot hidden></div>
          <div class="gfinder__includes" data-gf-includes hidden>
            <span class="gfinder__includes-label">Your ritual</span>
            <ol class="gfinder__includes-list" data-gf-includes-list></ol>
          </div>
          <div class="gfinder__why" data-gf-why hidden></div>
        </div>
        <div class="gfinder__explain" data-gf-explain hidden></div>
        <p class="gfinder__secondary" data-gf-secondary hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
(function () {
  var root = document.querySelector('[data-gfinder]');
  if (!root) return;

  var PRODUCTS = {
    velvet: {
      title: 'Velvet', subtitle: 'Foaming Cleanser',
      url: {{ velvet_prod.url | default: '/products/velvet' | json }},
      price: {{ velvet_prod.price | money | default: '' | json }},
      image: {{ img_velvet | asset_url | json }},
      variantId: {{ velvet_prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: null | json }}
    },
    silken: {
      title: 'Silken', subtitle: 'Skin Refining Gel',
      url: {{ silken_prod.url | default: '/products/silken' | json }},
      price: {{ silken_prod.price | money | default: '' | json }},
      image: {{ img_silken | asset_url | json }},
      variantId: {{ silken_prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: null | json }}
    },
    aura: {
      title: 'Aura', subtitle: 'Advanced Renewal Cream',
      url: {{ aura_prod.url | default: '/products/aura' | json }},
      price: {{ aura_prod.price | money | default: '' | json }},
      image: {{ img_aura | asset_url | json }},
      variantId: {{ aura_prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: null | json }}
    },
    veil: {
      title: 'Veil', subtitle: 'Renewing Serum',
      url: {{ veil_prod.url | default: '/products/veil' | json }},
      price: {{ veil_prod.price | money | default: '' | json }},
      image: {{ img_veil | asset_url | json }},
      variantId: {{ veil_prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: null | json }}
    },
    cashmere: {
      title: 'Cashmere', subtitle: 'Lightweight Hydrating Lotion',
      url: {{ cashmere_prod.url | default: '/products/cashmere' | json }},
      price: {{ cashmere_prod.price | money | default: '' | json }},
      image: {{ img_cashmere | asset_url | json }},
      variantId: {{ cashmere_prod.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | default: null | json }}
    }
  };

  // Q1 answer -> Ritual
  var RITUAL = {
    'Hydration': 'Hydration',
    'Texture': 'Refining',
    'Appearance of Fine Lines': 'Renewal',
    'Uneven Tones': 'Refining',
    'Appearance of Scars': 'Refining',
    'Overall Skin Maintenance': 'Essential'
  };

  // Q4 answer -> Tier
  var TIER = {
    'Keep It Simple': 'Essential',
    'Balanced Routine': 'Balanced',
    'Give Me The Full Ritual': 'Complete'
  };

  // Ritual x Tier -> displayed name + product set
  var MATRIX = {
    Essential: {
      Essential: { name: 'Essential Core',      items: ['velvet', 'cashmere'] },
      Balanced:  { name: 'Essential Plus',      items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'cashmere'] },
      Complete:  { name: 'Complete Core',       items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'cashmere'] }
    },
    Hydration: {
      Essential: { name: 'Hydration Essential', items: ['velvet', 'cashmere'] },
      Balanced:  { name: 'Hydration Balanced',  items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'cashmere'] },
      Complete:  { name: 'Hydration Complete',  items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'cashmere'] }
    },
    Refining: {
      Essential: { name: 'Refining Essential',  items: ['velvet', 'silken'] },
      Balanced:  { name: 'Refining Balanced',   items: ['velvet', 'silken', 'aura', 'cashmere'] },
      Complete:  { name: 'Refining Complete',   items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'silken', 'aura', 'cashmere'] }
    },
    Renewal: {
      Essential: { name: 'Renewal Essential',   items: ['velvet', 'aura'] },
      Balanced:  { name: 'Renewal Balanced',    items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'cashmere'] },
      Complete:  { name: 'Renewal Complete',    items: ['velvet', 'veil', 'aura', 'silken', 'cashmere'] }
    }
  };

  // Product set -> the bundle product's variant, where one has been chosen in
  // the theme editor. Empty entries fall back to adding the components.
  // Keyed per outcome (Ritual|Tier), not per product set, because two outcomes
  // can share identical contents and still be sold as separately named bundles
  // — Essential Core and Hydration Essential are both Velvet + Cashmere.
  var BUNDLES = {};
  {%- assign bundle_cells = 'Essential|Essential,Essential|Balanced,Essential|Complete,Hydration|Essential,Hydration|Balanced,Hydration|Complete,Refining|Essential,Refining|Balanced,Refining|Complete,Renewal|Essential,Renewal|Balanced,Renewal|Complete' | split: ',' -%}
  {%- for cell_key in bundle_cells -%}
    {%- case forloop.index -%}
      {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_essential_core -%}
      {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_essential_plus -%}
      {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_complete_core -%}
      {%- when 4 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_hydration_essential -%}
      {%- when 5 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_hydration_balanced -%}
      {%- when 6 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_hydration_complete -%}
      {%- when 7 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_refining_essential -%}
      {%- when 8 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_refining_balanced -%}
      {%- when 9 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_refining_complete -%}
      {%- when 10 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_renewal_essential -%}
      {%- when 11 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_renewal_balanced -%}
      {%- when 12 -%}{%- assign bp = section.settings.bundle_renewal_complete -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
    {%- if bp != blank and bp.selected_or_first_available_variant != blank -%}
  BUNDLES[{{ cell_key | json }}] = { id: {{ bp.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }}, title: {{ bp.title | json }}, price: {{ bp.price | money | json }} };
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  // Product set -> its photographed lineup, keyed on the set sorted alphabetically
  // so the two Complete tiers (same five products, listed in a different order)
  // resolve to the same shot.
  var SET_IMAGE = {
    'cashmere,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-velvet-cashmere.jpg' | asset_url | json }},
    'aura,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-velvet-aura.jpg' | asset_url | json }},
    'silken,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-velvet-silken.jpg' | asset_url | json }},
    'aura,cashmere,veil,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-velvet-veil-aura-cashmere.jpg' | asset_url | json }},
    'aura,cashmere,silken,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-velvet-silken-aura-cashmere.jpg' | asset_url | json }},
    'aura,cashmere,silken,veil,velvet': {{ 'ritual-set-full-five.jpg' | asset_url | json }}
  };

  // Q5 answer -> secondary product. Saved to the payload; it does not change
  // the set above. "Nothing else" maps to no secondary rather than dead-ending
  // the way the GHL workflow currently does.
  var SECONDARY = {
    'Hydration': 'cashmere',
    'Texture': 'silken',
    'Appearance of fine lines': 'aura',
    'Uneven tone': 'veil',
    'Appearance of scars': 'silken',
    'Overall skin maintenance': null,
    'Nothing else, just my primary goal': null
  };

  var steps    = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-gf-step]'));
  var contact  = root.querySelector('[data-gf-contact]');
  var screens  = steps.concat([contact]);
  var progress = root.querySelector('[data-gf-progress]');
  var curEl    = root.querySelector('[data-gf-current]');
  var totalEl  = root.querySelector('[data-gf-total]');
  var barEl    = root.querySelector('[data-gf-bar]');
  var backBtn  = root.querySelector('[data-gf-back]');
  var nav      = root.querySelector('[data-gf-nav]');
  var result   = root.querySelector('[data-gf-result]');
  var answers  = {};
  var index    = 0;
  var chosen   = null;

  if (totalEl) totalEl.textContent = String(steps.length);

  function show(i) {
    index = i;
    screens.forEach(function (s, n) { if (s) s.hidden = n !== i; });
    var onQuestions = i < steps.length;
    if (progress) progress.hidden = !onQuestions;
    if (onQuestions) {
      if (curEl) curEl.textContent = String(i + 1);
      if (barEl) barEl.style.width = (((i + 1) / steps.length) * 100) + '%';
    }
    if (backBtn) backBtn.hidden = i === 0;
    if (nav) nav.hidden = false;
  }

  // Q1 fixes the Ritual, which narrows the outcome to that row's three cells —
  // at most three distinct shots. Fetching them now means the result image is
  // already in cache by the time the visitor reaches it, five questions later.
  var warmed = {};
  function preloadFor(ritualAnswer) {
    var row = MATRIX[RITUAL[ritualAnswer]];
    if (!row) return;
    Object.keys(row).forEach(function (tier) {
      var src = SET_IMAGE[row[tier].items.slice().sort().join(',')];
      if (src && !warmed[src]) { warmed[src] = true; new Image().src = src; }
    });
  }

  steps.forEach(function (step, i) {
    var key = step.getAttribute('data-gf-key');
    step.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var btn = e.target.closest('[data-gf-opt]');
      if (!btn) return;
      answers[key] = btn.getAttribute('data-gf-opt');
      if (key === 'improve') preloadFor(answers[key]);
      step.querySelectorAll('[data-gf-opt]').forEach(function (b) {
        b.classList.toggle('is-chosen', b === btn);
      });
      show(i + 1);
    });
  });

  if (backBtn) {
    backBtn.addEventListener('click', function () { if (index > 0) show(index - 1); });
  }

  function resolve() {
    var ritual = RITUAL[answers.improve] || 'Essential';
    var tier   = TIER[answers.routine_fit] || 'Essential';
    var cell   = MATRIX[ritual][tier];
    var setKey = cell.items.slice().sort().join(',');
    var bundle = BUNDLES[ritual + '|' + tier] || null;
    return {
      ritual: ritual,
      tier: tier,
      // cell.name is the name from the logic document; bundle.title is what the
      // customer will see in the cart. Show the bundle's, so the result and the
      // cart do not print two different names for the same thing.
      name: bundle ? bundle.title : cell.name,
      matrixName: cell.name,
      bundle: bundle,
      items: cell.items,
      image: SET_IMAGE[setKey] || null,
      secondary: SECONDARY[answers.secondary] || null
    };
  }


  // ---- Personalised explanation ---------------------------------------------
  // Copy comes from the "Ritual Finder: Personalized Results & Explanation
  // Brief". Built from modules, as its section 14 asks, not one page per answer
  // combination: configuration -> core explanation, secondary goal -> supporting
  // line, skin type and sensitivity -> a note, current routine -> a starting
  // point. Only primary goal and routine preference change the bundle; the
  // rest is acknowledged, never presented as a reason a product was chosen.
  var CORE_COPY = {
      "Essential Core": [
          "You told us you're focused on maintaining your skin rather than addressing one specific concern, and you prefer to keep your routine simple.",
          "So we built your ritual around the essentials: cleansing and hydration. Velvet gives your ritual its daily cleansing foundation, while Cashmere provides lightweight moisture to complete the routine.",
          "Nothing unnecessary. Just two purposeful steps designed for someone who wants a consistent skincare foundation without a complicated routine."
      ],
      "Essential Plus": [
          "You told us your priority is overall skin maintenance and that you're comfortable with a balanced routine.",
          "Rather than focusing heavily on one concern, we built your ritual to support several parts of a well-rounded skincare routine. Velvet provides the cleansing foundation, Veil adds a targeted serum step, Aura introduces advanced renewal, and Cashmere completes the ritual with lightweight hydration.",
          "The result is a more complete approach to everyday skincare without requiring every step in the Chemistrie collection."
      ],
      "Complete Core": [
          "You told us you're focused on overall skin maintenance and you're comfortable with a complete skincare ritual.",
          "We built your recommendation around the Chemistrie products that make sense for broad, everyday support: Velvet for cleansing, Veil as your serum step, Aura for advanced renewal, and Cashmere for lightweight hydration.",
          "You asked for a complete approach, but we still follow one important rule: more products aren't automatically better. We recommend only what belongs in your ritual."
      ],
      "Hydration Essential": [
          "You told us hydration is your priority, but you don't want an overly complicated routine.",
          "So we kept your ritual intentionally focused. Velvet provides the cleansing foundation, followed by Cashmere for lightweight hydration and moisture support.",
          "It's a streamlined ritual built around the concern you identified as most important, without adding steps you didn't ask for."
      ],
      "Hydration Balanced": [
          "You told us hydration is your primary goal and that a balanced routine fits your lifestyle.",
          "We started with a cleansing and hydration foundation, then added complementary steps for a more complete ritual. Velvet cleanses, Veil adds a weightless hydrating serum step, Aura provides advanced renewal, and Cashmere finishes the ritual with lightweight moisture.",
          "The result keeps hydration at the center while giving you a more comprehensive routine."
      ],
      "Hydration Complete": [
          "You told us hydration matters most and that you're comfortable with a more complete skincare ritual.",
          "Your recommendation layers complementary steps around hydration: Velvet as your cleansing foundation, Veil as a weightless hydrating serum, Aura for advanced renewal, and Cashmere for lightweight moisture.",
          "Although you're comfortable with a full routine, we haven't added products simply to create more steps. Your ritual stays focused on what best supports the priorities you shared with us."
      ],
      "Refining Essential": [
          "You told us skin refinement is your primary goal, but you'd rather keep your routine simple.",
          "That led us to a focused two-step ritual. Velvet provides your daily cleansing foundation, while Silken gives your routine a targeted refining step.",
          "Instead of surrounding that goal with a larger routine, we've kept the recommendation intentionally streamlined around the priority you identified."
      ],
      "Refining Balanced": [
          "You told us skin refinement is your primary goal and that you're comfortable with a balanced routine.",
          "So we built your ritual around targeted refinement without stopping there. Velvet provides your cleansing foundation, Silken supplies the targeted refining step, Aura adds advanced renewal, and Cashmere provides lightweight moisture.",
          "Together, those steps give your primary concern a clear place in the ritual while surrounding it with the foundational care of a more balanced routine."
      ],
      "Refining Complete": [
          "You told us skin refinement is your primary goal and that you want the most complete Chemistrie ritual.",
          "Your recommendation brings together all five steps: Velvet to cleanse, Veil as your serum step, Silken for targeted refinement, Aura for advanced renewal, and Cashmere for lightweight hydration.",
          "It's our most comprehensive ritual, built around your refining priority while giving each product a distinct role rather than adding steps without purpose."
      ],
      "Renewal Essential": [
          "You told us the appearance of fine lines is your primary concern and that you'd rather keep your skincare routine simple.",
          "That made Aura the natural focus of your ritual. Velvet provides your cleansing foundation, while Aura introduces the advanced renewal step most closely aligned with the goal you identified.",
          "Two intentional steps keep the routine manageable while staying centered on what matters most to you."
      ],
      "Renewal Balanced": [
          "You told us the appearance of fine lines is your primary concern and that a balanced routine fits your lifestyle.",
          "We centered your ritual around Aura, our advanced renewal cream, then surrounded it with complementary foundational steps. Velvet cleanses, Veil provides your serum step, and Cashmere adds lightweight hydration.",
          "This gives renewal a central role without turning your daily skincare into an unnecessarily complicated routine."
      ],
      "Renewal Complete": [
          "You told us renewal is your priority and that you're comfortable with a complete skincare ritual.",
          "So we've built your recommendation around Aura and surrounded it with the full Chemistrie system: Velvet to cleanse, Veil as your serum step, Silken for targeted refinement, Aura for advanced renewal, and Cashmere for lightweight hydration.",
          "It's the most comprehensive version of the Renewal Ritual, designed for someone who wants multiple complementary skincare steps rather than a minimalist routine."
      ]
  };
  var SECONDARY_COPY = {
      "Hydration": "You also told us hydration matters to you, so we kept moisture support in mind when considering your overall ritual.",
      "Texture": "You also identified texture as something you'd like to focus on, giving us another signal that refinement matters to you.",
      "Appearance of fine lines": "The appearance of fine lines is also on your mind, so renewal is an important consideration within your overall skincare approach.",
      "Uneven tone": "You also told us you'd like to focus on a more even-looking complexion, giving us another consideration as we shaped your ritual.",
      "Appearance of scars": "You also identified the appearance of a fully healed scar as a secondary priority, which we consider a targeted refinement goal.",
      "Nothing else, just my primary goal": "You told us you'd rather stay focused on your primary goal, so we haven't tried to solve concerns you didn't ask us to address."
  };
  var SKIN_COPY = {
      "Dry": "You described your skin as typically dry, which gives us useful context for how hydration fits into your overall ritual.",
      "Normal": "You described your skin as typically balanced, so your recommendation remains centered on the goals you identified rather than correcting for a specific skin-type concern.",
      "Combination": "You described your skin as combination, which is helpful context as you introduce and adjust the different steps in your ritual.",
      "Oily": "You described your skin as typically oily, so we've kept that context in mind without assuming that oily skin doesn't also benefit from thoughtful hydration.",
      "Not Sure": "Not sure of your skin type? That's completely fine. Your recommendation is primarily built around the goals and routine preferences you told us about."
  };
  var SENS_COPY = {
      "Rarely reacts": "You told us your skin rarely reacts to new skincare products, so you can introduce your ritual normally while still paying attention to how your skin responds.",
      "Occasionally becomes irritated or sensitive": "Because your skin can occasionally become irritated or sensitive, consider introducing your ritual gradually rather than starting every new step at once.",
      "Frequently becomes irritated or sensitive": "You told us your skin frequently becomes irritated or sensitive. Your ritual recommendation remains based on your goals, but we recommend introducing new products gradually and patch testing before incorporating the full ritual.",
      "I'm not sure": "If you're unsure how your skin responds to new products, introducing your ritual gradually can help you understand how your skin responds to each step."
  };
  var START_COPY = {
      "Cleanser only or very minimal": "Because you're coming from a simpler routine, don't feel like you need to introduce every step at once. Building consistency matters more than adding everything on day one.",
      "I don't currently have a consistent routine": "Because you're coming from a simpler routine, don't feel like you need to introduce every step at once. Building consistency matters more than adding everything on day one.",
      "Cleanser + moisturizer": "You already have the foundation of a routine. Your Chemistrie ritual builds from that familiar structure by introducing more targeted steps around the goals you identified.",
      "A few targeted products": "You're already comfortable using targeted skincare, so your ritual gives those steps a clearer structure and order around your primary goal.",
      "Full multi-step routine": "You're already comfortable with a multi-step routine. Your recommendation is designed to give those steps a more intentional structure around the priorities you shared."
  };

  // Brief section 7: the Refining family opens with the customer's own goal
  // instead of the generic "skin refinement".
  var REFINING_GOAL = {
    'Texture': "improving the look and feel of your skin's texture is your primary goal",
    'Uneven Tones': 'a more even-looking complexion is your primary goal',
    'Appearance of Scars': "you'd like to focus on the appearance of a fully healed scar"
  };

  // Same goal named twice (primary and secondary) is not worth a second line.
  var PRIMARY_KEY = { 'Hydration': 'h', 'Texture': 't', 'Appearance of Fine Lines': 'l', 'Uneven Tones': 'u', 'Appearance of Scars': 's', 'Overall Skin Maintenance': 'm' };
  var SECONDARY_KEY = { 'Hydration': 'h', 'Texture': 't', 'Appearance of fine lines': 'l', 'Uneven tone': 'u', 'Appearance of scars': 's', 'Overall skin maintenance': 'm' };

  // Brief section 5 and its worked example: what each product does in a ritual.
  var ROLE = {
    velvet:   ['Cleanse',  'Your daily cleansing foundation.'],
    veil:     ['Treat',    'A weightless hydrating serum step.'],
    silken:   ['Refine',   'Targeted refinement step when texture, uneven appearance, or fully healed scars are important.'],
    aura:     ['Renew',    'Your advanced renewal step.'],
    cashmere: ['Moisturize', 'Lightweight hydration to complete your ritual.']
  };

  function explainBlock(heading, paragraphs) {
    var wrap = document.createElement('div');
    wrap.className = 'gfinder__ex';
    var h = document.createElement('h4');
    h.className = 'gfinder__ex-h';
    h.textContent = heading;
    wrap.appendChild(h);
    paragraphs.forEach(function (t) {
      if (!t) return;
      var p = document.createElement('p');
      p.className = 'gfinder__ex-p';
      p.textContent = t;
      wrap.appendChild(p);
    });
    return wrap;
  }

  function renderExplain(res) {
    var box = root.querySelector('[data-gf-explain]');
    var why = root.querySelector('[data-gf-why]');
    if (!box) return;
    box.innerHTML = '';
    if (why) { why.innerHTML = ''; why.hidden = true; }

    var core = (CORE_COPY[res.matrixName] || []).slice();
    if (core.length && res.ritual === 'Refining' && REFINING_GOAL[answers.improve]) {
      core[0] = core[0].replace('skin refinement is your primary goal', REFINING_GOAL[answers.improve]);
    }
    if (core.length) {
      // the core card sits beside the photo and list; the rest go in the row below
      var coreCard = explainBlock('Why we chose this ritual for you', core);
      if (why) { why.appendChild(coreCard); why.hidden = false; } else { box.appendChild(coreCard); }
    }

    var sec = SECONDARY_COPY[answers.secondary];
    var samePrimary = PRIMARY_KEY[answers.improve] && PRIMARY_KEY[answers.improve] === SECONDARY_KEY[answers.secondary];
    if (sec && !samePrimary) box.appendChild(explainBlock('You also told us\u2026', [sec]));

    var note = [SKIN_COPY[answers.skin_type], SENS_COPY[answers.sensitivity]].filter(Boolean);
    if (note.length) box.appendChild(explainBlock('A note about your skin', note));

    var start = START_COPY[answers.current_routine];
    if (start) box.appendChild(explainBlock('Your starting point', [start]));

    box.hidden = box.children.length === 0;
  }

  function render(res) {
    root.querySelector('[data-gf-result-title]').textContent = res.name;
    var eyebrow = root.querySelector('[data-gf-result-eyebrow]');
    if (eyebrow) eyebrow.textContent = (res.matrixName && res.matrixName !== res.name) ? 'Your ' + res.matrixName + ' ritual' : 'Your ritual';

    var shot = root.querySelector('[data-gf-shot]');
    if (res.image) {
      // eager, not lazy: by the time this renders the image is the thing the
      // visitor is waiting on, and it has been warmed by preloadFor() already.
      shot.innerHTML = '<img src="' + res.image + '" alt="' + res.name + '" loading="eager" decoding="async">';
      shot.hidden = false;
    } else {
      shot.hidden = true;
    }

    /* Built from res.items, the same array the add-to-cart call uses, so the
       list can never disagree with what actually goes in the bag. Order is the
       order of use, as the configuration lists it. */
    var incWrap = root.querySelector('[data-gf-includes]');
    var incList = root.querySelector('[data-gf-includes-list]');
    if (incList) {
      incList.innerHTML = '';
      (res.items || []).forEach(function (key, i) {
        var p = PRODUCTS[key];
        if (!p) return;
        var role = ROLE[key] || ['', ''];
        var li = document.createElement('li');
        li.className = 'gfinder__includes-item';
        var num = document.createElement('span');
        num.className = 'gfinder__includes-num';
        num.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
        num.textContent = String(i + 1);
        var body = document.createElement('span');
        body.className = 'gfinder__includes-body';
        var name = document.createElement('span');
        name.className = 'gfinder__includes-name';
        name.textContent = p.title + (role[0] ? ' \u00b7 ' + role[0] : '');
        var sub = document.createElement('span');
        sub.className = 'gfinder__includes-sub';
        sub.textContent = role[1] || p.subtitle || '';
        body.appendChild(name);
        body.appendChild(sub);
        li.appendChild(num);
        li.appendChild(body);
        incList.appendChild(li);
      });
      if (incWrap) incWrap.hidden = incList.children.length === 0;
    }

    renderExplain(res);

    var secEl = root.querySelector('[data-gf-secondary]');
    if (res.secondary && PRODUCTS[res.secondary]) {
      secEl.textContent = 'Noted for later: ' + PRODUCTS[res.secondary].title + ', for your secondary focus.';
      secEl.hidden = false;
    } else {
      secEl.hidden = true;
    }

    steps.forEach(function (s) { s.hidden = true; });
    if (contact) contact.hidden = true;
    if (progress) progress.hidden = true;
    if (nav) nav.hidden = true;
    result.hidden = false;
    var cardEl = root.querySelector('.gfinder__card');
    if (cardEl) {
      var header = document.querySelector('.nav');
      var offset = header ? header.getBoundingClientRect().height : 0;
      window.scrollTo({ top: cardEl.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - offset - 12, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
  }

  var submitBtn = root.querySelector('[data-gf-submit]');
  if (submitBtn) {
    submitBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var nameEl  = root.querySelector('[data-gf-name]');
      var emailEl = root.querySelector('[data-gf-email]');
      var errEl   = root.querySelector('[data-gf-error]');
      var name    = (nameEl.value || '').trim();
      var email   = (emailEl.value || '').trim();

      if (!name || !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/.test(email)) {
        errEl.textContent = 'Please add your first name and a valid email address.';
        errEl.hidden = false;
        return;
      }
      errEl.hidden = true;

      chosen = resolve();
      var payload = {
        first_name: name,
        email: email,
        answers: answers,
        ritual: chosen.ritual,
        tier: chosen.tier,
        // the logic document's name, which the GHL workflow matches on — the
        // bundle's own name goes alongside it rather than replacing it.
        final_ritual_recommendation: chosen.matrixName,
        bundle_name: chosen.bundle ? chosen.bundle.title : null,
        ritual_configuration: chosen.items.map(function (k) { return PRODUCTS[k].title; }).join(' + '),
        secondary_product: chosen.secondary ? PRODUCTS[chosen.secondary].title : null
      };

      // The recommendation shows either way — the handoff is best-effort so a
      // failing endpoint never costs the visitor their result.
      var endpoint = root.getAttribute('data-endpoint');
      if (endpoint) {
        try {
          fetch(endpoint, {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify(payload)
          }).catch(function () {});
        } catch (e) {}
      }

      render(chosen);
    });
  }

  var addBtn = root.querySelector('[data-gf-add]');
  if (addBtn) {
    addBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (!chosen) return;

      // One line item if a bundle product has been set for this exact set,
      // otherwise the components individually. Means the quiz keeps working
      // before the bundles exist and switches over on its own once they do.
      var items = chosen.bundle
        ? [{ id: chosen.bundle.id, quantity: 1 }]
        : chosen.items
            .map(function (k) { return PRODUCTS[k].variantId; })
            .filter(Boolean)
            .map(function (id) { return { id: id, quantity: 1 }; });
      if (!items.length) { window.location.href = '/collections/all'; return; }
      addBtn.disabled = true;
      fetch('/cart/add.js', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ items: items })
      }).then(function () { window.location.href = '/cart'; })
        .catch(function () { addBtn.disabled = false; });
    });
  }

  var restart = root.querySelector('[data-gf-restart]');
  if (restart) {
    restart.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      answers = {}; chosen = null;
      root.querySelectorAll('.is-chosen').forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-chosen'); });
      result.hidden = true;
      show(0);
    });
  }

  show(0);
})();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
/* First thing on the gift page, with the hero gone. Tan band, paper card,
   forest type — palette tokens only. */
.gfinder {
  background: var(--c-tan-3);
  color: var(--c-forest);
  padding: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 40px) clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px);
}
.gfinder__inner { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; }
/* Several classes here set their own display, which overrides the browser's
   [hidden] rule - that is how "Question 6 of 6" stayed on screen under the
   result even though the script hides it. One guard for the whole section. */
.gfinder [hidden] { display: none !important; }
.gfinder__head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: clamp(22px, 2.8vw, 36px); }
.gfinder__title { margin: 12px 0 0; }
.display-h.gfinder__title { color: var(--c-forest); }
.display-h.gfinder__title em { color: var(--c-tan-2); }

.gfinder__card {
  background: var(--c-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--c-line-soft);
  border-radius: 26px;
  /* narrower side padding than vertical, to give the result shot more room */
  padding: clamp(26px, 3.6vw, 56px) clamp(20px, 2.8vw, 44px);
  /* softer and green-tinted now the band is light — a black shadow at .55
     muddied the tan around the card. */
  box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -34px rgba(26, 58, 45, .35);
}

.gfinder__progress { display: block; margin-bottom: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 34px); }
.gfinder__progress-label { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-tan-2); }
.gfinder__progress-track { display: block; height: 2px; margin-top: 10px; background: rgba(26, 58, 45, .12); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
.gfinder__progress-track i { display: block; height: 100%; width: 16.6%; background: var(--c-tan); transition: width .4s var(--ease-out); }

.gfinder__step { border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.gfinder__q {
  display: block; margin: 0 0 clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px); padding: 0;
  font-family: var(--ff-display); font-size: clamp(21px, 2.4vw, 30px);
  line-height: 1.2; color: var(--c-forest);
}
.gfinder__sub { margin: -8px 0 20px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--c-ink-soft); }

/* Two-up on the wider card so six options don't run as a tall single stack. */
.gfinder__opts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
.gfinder__opts button {
  appearance: none; cursor: pointer; text-align: left;
  font-family: inherit; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.35; color: var(--c-forest);
  background: var(--c-cream); border: 1px solid var(--c-line-soft); border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 17px 22px;
  transition: background .25s var(--ease-out), border-color .25s var(--ease-out), color .25s var(--ease-out);
}
.gfinder__opts button:hover { background: var(--c-tan-3); border-color: var(--c-tan-2); }
.gfinder__opts button.is-chosen { background: var(--c-forest); border-color: var(--c-forest); color: var(--c-cream); }

.gfinder__fields { display: grid; gap: 14px; }
.gfinder__field span { display: block; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-ink-mute); margin-bottom: 6px; }
.gfinder__fields { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
.gfinder__field input {
  width: 100%; font-family: inherit; font-size: 15px; color: var(--c-forest);
  background: var(--c-cream); border: 1px solid var(--c-line-soft); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 16px;
}
.gfinder__field input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--c-forest); }
.gfinder__error { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 13.5px; color: #7a2b2b; }
.gfinder__submit { margin-top: 20px; }

.gfinder__nav { margin-top: 22px; }
.gfinder__back {
  appearance: none; background: none; border: 0; cursor: pointer; padding: 0;
  font-family: inherit; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-ink-mute);
}
.gfinder__back:hover { color: var(--c-forest); }

.gfinder__result-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-tan-2); }
/* compound selector so this wins over .display-h's own margin: 16px 0 0
   regardless of stylesheet order — otherwise the top gap was whichever of
   the two loaded last. */
.display-h.gfinder__result-title { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 3vw, 42px); line-height: 1.05; }
/* Sources are 2080px, so this can be raised again without losing sharpness —
   2x holds up to 1040px. width/height auto means it scales whole, never crops. */
.gfinder__shot {
  max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto;
  border-radius: 18px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--c-cream);
}
.gfinder__shot img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

.gfinder__result-head {
  display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px 28px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-bottom: clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px);
}
.gfinder__result-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px; }
.gfinder__restart { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-ink-mute); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line); padding-bottom: 3px; }
.gfinder__restart:hover { color: var(--c-forest); border-color: var(--c-forest); }

/* photo | ritual list | why-we-chose card */
.gfinder__result-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
  gap: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 30px);
  align-items: start;
}
.gfinder__result-grid .gfinder__shot { max-width: none; margin: 0; }
.gfinder__includes-label { display: block; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-tan-2); margin-bottom: 10px; }
.gfinder__includes-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
/* A ruled column, not cards: these are the contents of one set, so they should
   read as rows of a single object rather than five things to choose between. */
.gfinder__includes-item { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line-soft); }
.gfinder__includes-num { flex: 0 0 auto; min-width: 16px; font-family: var(--ff-display); font-style: italic; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--c-tan-2); }
.gfinder__includes-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
.gfinder__includes-item:first-child { padding-top: 0; }
.gfinder__includes-item:last-child { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
.gfinder__includes-name { font-family: var(--ff-display); font-size: clamp(16px, 1.4vw, 18px); color: var(--c-forest); line-height: 1.2; }
.gfinder__includes-sub { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--c-ink-soft); }

/* Cards: the why-we-chose card in the middle row, the rest in one row below. */
.gfinder__explain {
  margin-top: clamp(16px, 2vw, 22px);
  display: flex;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: clamp(12px, 1.6vw, 20px);
}
.gfinder__ex {
  flex: 1 1 0;
  min-width: 0;
  background: var(--c-cream);
  border: 1px solid var(--c-line-soft);
  border-radius: 16px;
  padding: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 22px);
  box-shadow: 0 22px 44px -32px rgba(26, 58, 45, .38);
}
.gfinder__why .gfinder__ex { border-top: 3px solid var(--c-tan); }
.gfinder__ex-h { font-family: var(--ff-body); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-tan-2); margin: 0 0 8px; }
.gfinder__ex-p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--c-ink-soft); margin: 0 0 8px; }
.gfinder__ex-p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
/* the opening "You told us..." sentence is the headline of the why card */
.gfinder__why .gfinder__ex-p:first-of-type {
  font-family: var(--ff-display); font-style: italic;
  font-size: clamp(17px, 1.5vw, 19px); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--c-forest);
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.gfinder__secondary { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--c-ink-soft); font-style: italic; }

/* Below desktop the three columns get too narrow: photo and list side by side,
   the why card full width under them; then one column on phones. */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .gfinder__result-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .gfinder__why { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .gfinder__explain { flex-direction: column; }
}
@media (max-width: 760px) {
  .gfinder__result-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .gfinder__result-head { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
}

@media (max-width: 760px) {
  /* single column below the two-up breakpoint, for options and the name/email
     pair alike */
  .gfinder__opts, .gfinder__fields { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .gfinder__opts button { padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 14.5px; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Ritual Finder Quiz",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Ritual Finder" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Six questions.<br/><em>One ritual.</em>" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "webhook_url", "label": "Submission endpoint (optional)", "info": "Inbound webhook that receives the name, email, answers and recommendation — the GoHighLevel workflow's trigger URL. Leave blank and the quiz still shows the result on screen, but nothing is sent anywhere." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Bundles" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "One bundle per quiz outcome. Outcomes with the same formulas can still point at differently named bundles. Any left empty add their formulas individually instead, so these can be filled in one at a time." },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_essential_core", "label": "Essential Core", "info": "Velvet + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_essential_plus", "label": "Essential Plus", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_complete_core", "label": "Complete Core", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_hydration_essential", "label": "Hydration Essential", "info": "Velvet + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_hydration_balanced", "label": "Hydration Balanced", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_hydration_complete", "label": "Hydration Complete", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_refining_essential", "label": "Refining Essential", "info": "Velvet + Silken" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_refining_balanced", "label": "Refining Balanced", "info": "Velvet + Silken + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_refining_complete", "label": "Refining Complete", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Silken + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_renewal_essential", "label": "Renewal Essential", "info": "Velvet + Aura" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_renewal_balanced", "label": "Renewal Balanced", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Cashmere" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "bundle_renewal_complete", "label": "Renewal Complete", "info": "Velvet + Veil + Aura + Silken + Cashmere" }
